      "message": "If I don\u0027t comment it out, I get these error messages after adding a GenerateAndroidBuildActions to ModuleBase: \n\n      /usr/local/google/home/rbraunstein/aosp-main-with-phones/build/soong/android/filegroup.go:118:21: cannot use module (variable of type *FileGroupDefaults) as DefaultsModule value in argument to InitDefaultsModule: *FileGroupDefaults does not implement DefaultsModule (ambiguous selector *FileGroupDefaults.GenerateAndroidBuildActions)\n\n     /usr/local/google/home/rbraunstein/aosp-main-with-phones/build/soong/android/filegroup.go:120:9: cannot use module (variable of type *FileGroupDefaults) as Module value in return statement: *FileGroupDefaults does not implement Module (ambiguous selector *FileGroupDefaults.GenerateAndroidBuildActions)\n     \nCommenting the GenerateAndroidBuildAction in filegroup resolved the problem, but I\u0027m not sure it now InitDefaultsModule is still doing the right thing or calling methods on the wrong base class (all tests still pass and build still work ...)\n\nI\u0027d love to hear alternatives or know the right golang way to help.\nI think that this:\n```\n type DefaultsModule interface {\n\tModule\n\tDefaults\n}\n```\nis creating a new interface by composing those two interfaces.\nThis is ensuring that DefaultModuleBase (which declares GenerateAndroidBuildAction) fulfills the Defaults interface:\n`   var _ Defaults \u003d (*DefaultsModuleBase)(nil)`\n\nSo now our composed interface declases the same method twice (GeneratedAndroidBuildActions).  I removed the one from the implementation that doesn\u0027t do anything.  I\u0027m not sure why it was there to begin with.\n\nAnd I made a change in filegroup to call ModuleBase.GenerateAndroidBuildActions\nhttps://android-review.git.corp.google.com/c/platform/build/soong/+/2883106/10/android/filegroup.go#96",
