      "side": 1,
      "message": "Properties don\u0027t typically have GenerateAndroidBuildActions methods on them.  Modules do.  So this should just go in ModuleBase.GenerateBuildActions.\n\nThe way this works is that android.ModuleBase implements blueprint\u0027s GenerateBuildActions, and does the default stuff, and then calls android.GenerateAndroidBuildActions. That way all of the built-in features of android.ModuleBase don\u0027t need to have the actual module types call all the \"superclass\" methods.\n\nIf you put this logic there, you don\u0027t have to touch every single module type and make sure it calls this method.",
      "revId": "cd59697c48e0618881cca453e167eee6a0e50f95",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
