      "message": "I was _only_ having ModuleBase.GenerateAndroidBuildActions calls this code.  All the \"subclasses\" were just calling their super for GenerateAndroidBuildActions.\nI moved it out to the property as well to make the code a little cleaner, but I\u0027m fine putting it in Base GenerateAndroidBuildActions directly.\n\ni.e. it looked like this:\n```\nfunc (m *ModuleBase) GenerateAndroidBuildActions(ctx ModuleContext) {\n\tm.teamProperties.GenerateAndroidBuildActions(ctx)\n}\n```\nand now it looks like:\n```\nfunc (m *ModuleBase) GenerateAndroidBuildActions(ctx ModuleContext) {\n\tm.generateActionsForTeamProto(ctx)\n}\n```\nbut the callers are exactly the same.\n\n\nFYI, I could be wrong, but I think I still do have to change every module to call super, like here in java: https://android-review.git.corp.google.com/c/platform/build/soong/+/2883106/10/java/java.go#717\n\nI tried it without making these change and it didn\u0027t work.  I had assumed I wouldn\u0027t need to and I spent a lot of time figuring out what the problem was.\n\ni.e  java or cc already GenerateAndroidBuildActions receivers.  There is no existing explicit calls to \"superclass\" one because it doesn\u0027t exist, doesn\u0027t do anything.  So in addition to adding it the superclass, I had to add the explicit calls.",
